897 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 531 0 R
/E ( The literature reviewed for this project highlights the growing global effort to strengthen transparency, accountability, and donor trust in the nonprofit sector through digital technologies. Almaghrabi et al. introduce a blockchain-based framework designed specifically for donation traceability, demonstrating how decentralized ledgers can eliminate manipulation and provide an immutable record of fund flow. Their work establishes the foundation for secure charitable ecosystems where donors can verify the end-use of contributions in real time. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
898 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 531 0 R
/E (Similarly, the study published in IJERT reinforces the role of blockchain in enhancing donation security. By implementing cryptographic methods and comparative analysis with traditional systems, the paper demonstrates how decentralized transaction records dramatically improve auditability and reduce fraudulent activities. Together, these blockchain-focused studies justify the need for transparent systems within NGO platforms like Connect2NGO. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
899 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
