/E (The Iterative SDLC Model is a cyclical approach to system development where the software is built and refined in successive versions. Each iteration includes phases such as requirement analysis, design, coding, and testing. At the end of every cycle, the prototype is reviewed, user feedback is gathered, and necessary modifications are incorporated before proceeding to the next stage. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1061 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (This methodology was particularly suited for Connect2NGO because of its multi-user environment and evolving functional requirements. Rather than attempting to build the entire system in one go, the team developed and validated each module in stages. For instance, modules for NGO registration, donor engagement, volunteer management, and admin analytics were each created and tested separately before being integrated into the unified platform. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
